LOCKED SCORING (Phase 1):
- Candidate match score S = sum(score_i * weight_i) / sum(weight_i), weights: Name 0.35, Identifier 0.30, Date of birth 0.10, Birth year 0.05, Country 0.05, Entity type 0.05, Gender 0.10.
- Classification: S >= 0.85 MATCH, 0.65 <= S < 0.85 POSSIBLE_MATCH, S < 0.65 NO_MATCH.
- CRI = [1 - product(1 - (S_i * W_i))] * 100 (probabilistic complement-product across sources, never an average or max). Per-source weights W_i are NOT locked yet.
- The LLM only reviews borderline POSSIBLE_MATCH cases and writes explanations; formulas and rules decide, the LLM never decides a match alone.
- Only matches and possible matches above threshold are stored; sources are discovered dynamically (nothing hardcoded per country or provider), e.g. if someone is not on OFAC but is on a Ghana domestic list, it should still show.
- Data sources: OpenSanctions API (sanctions and PEP, aggregates 100+ lists) plus web search; adverse media uses web/news search.

